"image": "/11909/11909_ms16800_1_14_010_thumb.jpg", "page": "14", "label": "10", "href": "/paper-summary/ordinance-14-november-1842/14"}, {"image": "/11909/11909_ms16800_1_14_011_thumb.jpg", "page": "15", "label": "11", "href": "/paper-summary/ordinance-14-november-1842/15"}, {"image": "/11909/11909_ms16800_1_14_012_thumb.jpg", "page": "16", "label": "12", "href": "/paper-summary/ordinance-14-november-1842/16"}, {"image": "/11909/11909_ms16800_1_14_013_thumb.jpg", "page": "17", "label": "13", "href": "/paper-summary/ordinance-14-november-1842/17"}, {"image": "/11909/11909_ms16800_1_14_014_thumb.jpg", "page": "18", "label": "14", "href": "/paper-summary/ordinance-14-november-1842/18"}, {"image": "/11909/11909_ms16800_1_14_015_thumb.jpg", "page": "19", "label": "15", "href": "/paper-summary/ordinance-14-november-1842/19"}, {"image": "/11909/11909_ms16800_1_14_016_thumb.jpg", "page": "20", "label": "16", "href": "/paper-summary/ordinance-14-november-1842/20"}, {"image": "/11909/11909_ms16800_1_14_017_thumb.jpg", "page": "21", "label": "17", "href": "/paper-summary/ordinance-14-november-1842/21"}, {"image": "/11909/11909_ms16800_1_14_018_thumb.jpg", "page": "22", "label": "18", "href": "/paper-summary/ordinance-14-november-1842/22"}, {"image": "/11909/11909_ms16800_1_14_019_thumb.jpg", "page": "23", "label": "[19]", "href": "/paper-summary/ordinance-14-november-1842/23"}, {"image": "/11909/11909_ms16800_1_14_020_thumb.jpg", "page": "24", "label": "[20]", "href": "/paper-summary/ordinance-14-november-1842/24"}], "tableOfContents": [], "summary": {"uri": "ordinance-14-november-1842", "series": "JSPPA", "urlTitleValue": "JSPPA6", "documentSeriesIdCompiled": "jsppa6-sub-nccr-sub02-421114", "documentSeriesUri": "/the-papers/administrative-records/jsppa6/jsppa6-sub-nccr/jsppa6-sub-nccr-sub02/jsppa6-sub-nccr-sub02-421114", "documentSeriesTitle": "<p>\r\n\tMeeting, 14 November 1842</p>", "editorialPageNumber": "11", "isPageNumberPresent": true, "searchUrl": "/published/jsp/searchable/papers/54016763/54016763-0015.xml", "clearText": "<html><head></head><body><div class=\"indent wasptag\"><aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"5394332373598765383\"><a href=\"#5394332373598765383\" class=\"new-scribe-note staticPopup\" title=\"New Scribe\" name=\"trans2\"><img src=\"//cdn.churchofjesuschrist.org/ch/jsp/images/icn-new-scribe-16.png\" alt=\"Indicates a change in handwriting to a different scribe.\"></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\"><a href=\"/person/james-sloan\" class=\"referenceInPop\">James Sloan</a> handwriting ends; first unidentified scribe begins.</p><hr></div></div></aside>Section 6. It shall not be lawful for the municipal Court on a scecond writ of <aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"11245632699030221983\"><a href=\"#11245632699030221983\" class=\"reference staticPopup\" ro=\"x41899\" topic=\"x41899\" title=\"Habeas corpus\">Habeas Corpus</a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data\" isnote=\"Y\" isnonsearchable=\"Y\"><input type=\"hidden\" value=\"Habeas corpus\"><p>“Have the body”; a written order from a court of competent jurisdiction commanding anyone having a person in custody to produce such person at a certain time and place and to state the reasons why he or she is being held in custody. The court will determine...</p><a class=\"more\" href=\"/topic/habeas-corpus\">View Glossary</a></div></div></aside> obtained by such prisoner or prisoners<aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"8230127360468061901\"><a href=\"#8230127360468061901\" class=\"new-scribe-note staticPopup\" title=\"New Scribe\" name=\"trans3\"><img src=\"//cdn.churchofjesuschrist.org/ch/jsp/images/icn-new-scribe-16.png\" alt=\"Indicates a change in handwriting to a different scribe.\"></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">Insertion in graphite. This and all insertions until the end of the document are in the handwriting of <a href=\"/person/james-sloan\" class=\"referenceInPop\">James Sloan</a> unless otherwise noted.</p><hr></div></div></aside> or prisoners <span class=\"josephswriting\">to discharge the </span>Said<aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"2378930593470823832\"><a href=\"#2378930593470823832\" class=\"new-scribe-note staticPopup\" title=\"New Scribe\" name=\"trans4\"><img src=\"//cdn.churchofjesuschrist.org/ch/jsp/images/icn-new-scribe-16.png\" alt=\"Indicates a change in handwriting to a different scribe.\"></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">Insertion in the handwriting of first unidentified scribe.</p><hr></div></div></aside> <span class=\"josephswriting\">prisoner </span><aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"3144253574150207347\"><a href=\"#3144253574150207347\" class=\"new-scribe-note staticPopup\" title=\"New Scribe\" name=\"trans5\"><img src=\"//cdn.churchofjesuschrist.org/ch/jsp/images/icn-new-scribe-16.png\" alt=\"Indicates a change in handwriting to a different scribe.\"></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">Insertion in the handwriting of JS.</p><hr></div></div></aside><span class=\"josephswriting\"> </span>or prisoners<aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"16833786959771159696\"><a href=\"#16833786959771159696\" class=\"new-scribe-note staticPopup\" title=\"New Scribe\" name=\"trans6\"><img src=\"//cdn.churchofjesuschrist.org/ch/jsp/images/icn-new-scribe-16.png\" alt=\"Indicates a change in handwriting to a different scribe.\"></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\"><a href=\"/person/james-sloan\" class=\"referenceInPop\">James Sloan</a> overwrote and replaced JS’s original insertion.</p><hr></div></div></aside> if he she or they <span class=\"josephswriting\">are</span><aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"14904784041699035752\"><a href=\"#14904784041699035752\" class=\"new-scribe-note staticPopup\" title=\"New Scribe\" name=\"trans7\"><img src=\"//cdn.churchofjesuschrist.org/ch/jsp/images/icn-new-scribe-16.png\" alt=\"Indicates a change in handwriting to a different scribe.\"></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">Insertion in the handwriting of JS.</p><hr></div></div></aside><span class=\"josephswriting\"> </span>proven Guilty of the charges clearly and specificaly charged in the warrant of commitment, with a criminal offence: but if the prisoner or prisoners shall be found guilty the Municipal Court shall only admit such prisoner or prisoners to Bail <span class=\"josephswriting\">where</span><aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"8371475635236184569\"><a href=\"#8371475635236184569\" class=\"new-scribe-note staticPopup\" title=\"New Scribe\" name=\"trans8\"><img src=\"//cdn.churchofjesuschrist.org/ch/jsp/images/icn-new-scribe-16.png\" alt=\"Indicates a change in handwriting to a different scribe.\"></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">Insertion in the handwriting of JS.</p><hr></div></div></aside><span class=\"josephswriting\"> </span> the offence is Bailable by Law, or ordinance, or remand him her or them to prison where the offence is not Bailable, or being bailable, if<aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"10920872443995425102\"><a href=\"#10920872443995425102\" class=\"new-scribe-note staticPopup\" title=\"New Scribe\" name=\"trans9\"><img src=\"//cdn.churchofjesuschrist.org/ch/jsp/images/icn-new-scribe-16.png\" alt=\"Indicates a change in handwriting to a different scribe.\"></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">Insertion in the handwriting of first unidentified scribe.</p><hr></div></div></aside> such prisoner or prisoners shall fail to give the Bail required.<aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"3016803777621117220\"><a href=\"#3016803777621117220\" class=\"editorial-note-static staticPopup\" title=\"Note\" name=\"trans18\"><span id=\"documenttrans18\">18</span></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">Section 6 of the state statute forbade courts from discharging a prisoner on a second writ of <a href=\"/topic/habeas-corpus\" class=\"referenceInPop\">habeas corpus</a> if he or she was charged with a criminal offence. The Nauvoo City Council added the clauses “are proven Guilty of the charges” and “if the prisoner or prisoners shall be found guilty” to the city ordinance, thus further empowering the municipal court to look behind the charges, as described above. These additions suggest that the city council misunderstood the purpose of habeas corpus, as they imply that the court would be determining guilt or innocence through the proceedings. (An Act . . . on Writs of Habeas Corpus, p. 325, sec. 6.)</p><hr><div class=\"works-cited-links\"><a href=\"/works-cited\" class=\"pdf\" id=\"comp-works\">Comprehensive Works Cited</a></div><div class=\"source-note\"><p id=\"source-note1\"><span class=\"title\">The Revised Code of Laws, of Illinois, Enacted at the Fifth General Assembly, at Their Session Held at Vandalia, Commencing on the Fourth Day of December, 1826, and Ending the Nineteenth of February, 1827.</span> Vandalia, IL: Robert Blackwell, 1827.</p></div></div></div></aside></div> <div class=\"indent wasptag\">Section 7 No person or persons<aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"11790856117502854819\"><a href=\"#11790856117502854819\" class=\"new-scribe-note staticPopup\" title=\"New Scribe\" name=\"trans10\"><img src=\"//cdn.churchofjesuschrist.org/ch/jsp/images/icn-new-scribe-16.png\" alt=\"Indicates a change in handwriting to a different scribe.\"></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">Insertion in the handwriting of first unidentified scribe.</p><hr></div></div></aside> who have<aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"2219288783957145058\"><a href=\"#2219288783957145058\" class=\"new-scribe-note staticPopup\" title=\"New Scribe\" name=\"trans11\"><img src=\"//cdn.churchofjesuschrist.org/ch/jsp/images/icn-new-scribe-16.png\" alt=\"Indicates a change in handwriting to a different scribe.\"></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">Insertion in the handwriting of first unidentified scribe.</p><hr></div></div></aside> been discharged by order of the Municipal Court on a Habeas Corpus, shall be again imprisoned, restrained, or kept in Custody for the same Cause, unless he, she or they, be afterwards indicted for the same offence, or unless by the [p. 11]</div></body></html>", "expandedText": "<html><head></head><body><div class=\"indent wasptag\"><aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"11362814020976159784\"><a href=\"#11362814020976159784\" class=\"new-scribe-note staticPopup\" title=\"New Scribe\" name=\"trans2\"><img src=\"//cdn.churchofjesuschrist.org/ch/jsp/images/icn-new-scribe-16.png\" alt=\"Indicates a change in handwriting to a different scribe.\"></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\"><a href=\"/person/james-sloan\" class=\"referenceInPop\">James Sloan</a> handwriting ends; first unidentified scribe begins.</p><hr></div></div></aside>Section 6. It shall not be lawful for the<aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"13253934796583874657\"><a href=\"#13253934796583874657\" class=\"editorial-note-static staticPopup\" title=\"Note\" name=\"trans17\"><span id=\"documenttrans17\">17</span></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">TEXT: Curlicues were used to finish the rest of this line, presumably to foreclose the possibility of adding further text.</p><hr></div></div></aside> <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>municipal Court on a scecond writ of <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span><aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"15735209691478667332\"><a href=\"#15735209691478667332\" class=\"reference staticPopup\" ro=\"x41899\" topic=\"x41899\" title=\"Habeas corpus\">Habeas Corpus</a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data\" isnote=\"Y\" isnonsearchable=\"Y\"><input type=\"hidden\" value=\"Habeas corpus\"><p>“Have the body”; a written order from a court of competent jurisdiction commanding anyone having a person in custody to produce such person at a certain time and place and to state the reasons why he or she is being held in custody. The court will determine...</p><a class=\"more\" href=\"/topic/habeas-corpus\">View Glossary</a></div></div></aside> obtained by such prisoner &lt;​or prisoners​&gt;<aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"13122512280521409713\"><a href=\"#13122512280521409713\" class=\"new-scribe-note staticPopup\" title=\"New Scribe\" name=\"trans3\"><img src=\"//cdn.churchofjesuschrist.org/ch/jsp/images/icn-new-scribe-16.png\" alt=\"Indicates a change in handwriting to a different scribe.\"></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">Insertion in graphite. This and all insertions until the end of the document are in the handwriting of <a href=\"/person/james-sloan\" class=\"referenceInPop\">James Sloan</a> unless otherwise noted.</p><hr></div></div></aside> <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>or prisoners &lt;​<span class=\"josephswriting\">to discharge the </span>&lt;​Said​&gt;<aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"7989059056717910046\"><a href=\"#7989059056717910046\" class=\"new-scribe-note staticPopup\" title=\"New Scribe\" name=\"trans4\"><img src=\"//cdn.churchofjesuschrist.org/ch/jsp/images/icn-new-scribe-16.png\" alt=\"Indicates a change in handwriting to a different scribe.\"></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">Insertion in the handwriting of first unidentified scribe.</p><hr></div></div></aside> <span class=\"josephswriting\">prisoner </span><span class=\"deleted\"><span class=\"josephswriting\">or prison</span><span class=\"illegible\">◊</span></span>​&gt;<aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"5030802365220868726\"><a href=\"#5030802365220868726\" class=\"new-scribe-note staticPopup\" title=\"New Scribe\" name=\"trans5\"><img src=\"//cdn.churchofjesuschrist.org/ch/jsp/images/icn-new-scribe-16.png\" alt=\"Indicates a change in handwriting to a different scribe.\"></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">Insertion in the handwriting of JS.</p><hr></div></div></aside><span class=\"josephswriting\"> </span>&lt;​or prisoners​&gt;<aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"13487475049400922756\"><a href=\"#13487475049400922756\" class=\"new-scribe-note staticPopup\" title=\"New Scribe\" name=\"trans6\"><img src=\"//cdn.churchofjesuschrist.org/ch/jsp/images/icn-new-scribe-16.png\" alt=\"Indicates a change in handwriting to a different scribe.\"></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\"><a href=\"/person/james-sloan\" class=\"referenceInPop\">James Sloan</a> overwrote and replaced JS’s original insertion.</p><hr></div></div></aside> if he &lt;​she​&gt; or they <span class=\"deleted\">is</span> &lt;​<span class=\"josephswriting\">are</span>​&gt;<aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"16623387462686388863\"><a href=\"#16623387462686388863\" class=\"new-scribe-note staticPopup\" title=\"New Scribe\" name=\"trans7\"><img src=\"//cdn.churchofjesuschrist.org/ch/jsp/images/icn-new-scribe-16.png\" alt=\"Indicates a change in handwriting to a different scribe.\"></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">Insertion in the handwriting of JS.</p><hr></div></div></aside><span class=\"josephswriting\"> </span>proven Guilty of the <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>charges clearly and specificaly charged in the <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>warrant of commitment, with a criminal <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>offence: but if the prisoner or prisoners shall be <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>found guilty the Mun[i]cipal Court shall only <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>admit such prisoner or prisoners to Bail &lt;​<span class=\"josephswriting\">where</span>​&gt;<aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"7899123066019996443\"><a href=\"#7899123066019996443\" class=\"new-scribe-note staticPopup\" title=\"New Scribe\" name=\"trans8\"><img src=\"//cdn.churchofjesuschrist.org/ch/jsp/images/icn-new-scribe-16.png\" alt=\"Indicates a change in handwriting to a different scribe.\"></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">Insertion in the handwriting of JS.</p><hr></div></div></aside><span class=\"josephswriting\"> </span><span class=\"deleted\">were</span> <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>the offence is Bailable by Law, or ordinance, <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>or remand him &lt;​her​&gt; or them to <span class=\"deleted\">the</span> prison where the <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>offence is not Bailable&lt;​, or being bailable,​&gt; &lt;​if​&gt;<aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"17166470754628120256\"><a href=\"#17166470754628120256\" class=\"new-scribe-note staticPopup\" title=\"New Scribe\" name=\"trans9\"><img src=\"//cdn.churchofjesuschrist.org/ch/jsp/images/icn-new-scribe-16.png\" alt=\"Indicates a change in handwriting to a different scribe.\"></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">Insertion in the handwriting of first unidentified scribe.</p><hr></div></div></aside> such prisoner or prisoners <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>shall fail to give the Bail required.<aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"14536260994903166043\"><a href=\"#14536260994903166043\" class=\"editorial-note-static staticPopup\" title=\"Note\" name=\"trans18\"><span id=\"documenttrans18\">18</span></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">Section 6 of the state statute forbade courts from discharging a prisoner on a second writ of <a href=\"/topic/habeas-corpus\" class=\"referenceInPop\">habeas corpus</a> if he or she was charged with a criminal offence. The Nauvoo City Council added the clauses “are proven Guilty of the charges” and “if the prisoner or prisoners shall be found guilty” to the city ordinance, thus further empowering the municipal court to look behind the charges, as described above. These additions suggest that the city council misunderstood the purpose of habeas corpus, as they imply that the court would be determining guilt or innocence through the proceedings. (An Act . . . on Writs of Habeas Corpus, p. 325, sec. 6.)</p><hr><div class=\"works-cited-links\"><a href=\"/works-cited\" class=\"pdf\" id=\"comp-works\">Comprehensive Works Cited</a></div><div class=\"source-note\"><p id=\"source-note1\"><span class=\"title\">The Revised Code of Laws, of Illinois, Enacted at the Fifth General Assembly, at Their Session Held at Vandalia, Commencing on the Fourth Day of December, 1826, and Ending the Nineteenth of February, 1827.</span> Vandalia, IL: Robert Blackwell, 1827.</p></div></div></div></aside></div> <div class=\"indent wasptag\">Section 7<span class=\"superscript\"><span class=\"deleted\">th</span></span> No person &lt;​or persons​&gt;<aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"8596433840748689106\"><a href=\"#8596433840748689106\" class=\"new-scribe-note staticPopup\" title=\"New Scribe\" name=\"trans10\"><img src=\"//cdn.churchofjesuschrist.org/ch/jsp/images/icn-new-scribe-16.png\" alt=\"Indicates a change in handwriting to a different scribe.\"></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">Insertion in the handwriting of first unidentified scribe.</p><hr></div></div></aside> who <span class=\"deleted\">has</span> &lt;​have​&gt;<aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"5817252757057087246\"><a href=\"#5817252757057087246\" class=\"new-scribe-note staticPopup\" title=\"New Scribe\" name=\"trans11\"><img src=\"//cdn.churchofjesuschrist.org/ch/jsp/images/icn-new-scribe-16.png\" alt=\"Indicates a change in handwriting to a different scribe.\"></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">Insertion in the handwriting of first unidentified scribe.</p><hr></div></div></aside> been discharged by order <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>of the Municipal Court on a Habeas Corpus, shall <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>be again imprisoned, restrained, or kept in Custody <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>for the same Cause, unless he, she or they, be after<span class=\"line-break hyphenate\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>wards indicted for the same offence, or unless by the [p. 11]</div></body></html>", "calendarsOfDocuments": [], "versions": [{"versionTitle": "Ordinance, 14 November 1842", "versionLink": "/paper-summary/ordinance-14-november-1842/1", "versionFeatured": ""}, {"versionTitle": "Nauvoo City Council Minute Book, 1841–1845", "versionLink": "/paper-summary/nauvoo-city-council-minute-book-1841-1845/125", "versionFeatured": ""}, {"versionTitle": "Ordinance, 14 November 1842, as Published in the <em xmlns:tei=\"http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0\" xmlns:lds=\"https://ldsc.xmlref.com/local/ldschurch\">Wasp</em>", "versionLink": "/paper-summary/ordinance-14-november-1842-as-published-in-the-wasp/1", "versionFeatured": ""}, {"versionTitle": "History, 1838–1856, volume D-1 [1 August 1842–1 July 1843]", "versionLink": "/paper-summary/history-1838-1856-volume-d-1-1-august-1842-1-july-1843/58", "versionFeatured": ""}, {"versionTitle": "“History of Joseph Smith”", "versionLink": "/paper-summary/history-of-joseph-smith/451", "versionFeatured": ""}], "images": {"smallImageUrl": "/11909/11909_ms16800_1_14_011_thumb.jpg", "mediumImageUrl": "/11909/11909_ms16800_1_14_011_med.jpg", "largeImageUrl": "/11909/11909_ms16800_1_14_011.jpg", "downloadImageUrl": "/11909/11909_ms16800_1_14_011_download.jpg"}, "imageCredit": "", "facsimile": "", "dzUrlXml": "/11909/11909_ms16800_1_14_011.xml", "classification": "Administrative", "publishedStatus": "FinalContent", "accessionNumber": "11909", "requestedPageNumber": "15", "numberOfPages": "24", "editorialTitle": "Ordinance, 14 November 1842", "cleanEditorialTitle": "Ordinance, 14 November 1842", "date": "November 14, 1842", "handwriting": "Handwriting of James Sloan, two unidentified scribes, and JS", "footnotes": [{"id": "11362814020976159784", "text": "<html><head></head><body><p class=\"bottom_0\"><a href=\"/person/james-sloan\" class=\"referenceInPop\">James Sloan</a> handwriting ends; first unidentified scribe begins.</p></body></html>", "number": null, "type": "scribal", "toenote": "", "longcitation": null}, {"id": "13253934796583874657", "text": "<html><head></head><body><p class=\"bottom_0\">TEXT: Curlicues were used to finish the rest of this line, presumably to foreclose the possibility of adding further text.</p></body></html>", "number": 17, "type": "number", "toenote": "", "longcitation": null}, {"id": "13122512280521409713", "text": "<html><head></head><body><p class=\"bottom_0\">Insertion in graphite. This and all insertions until the end of the document are in the handwriting of <a href=\"/person/james-sloan\" class=\"referenceInPop\">James Sloan</a> unless otherwise noted.</p></body></html>", "number": null, "type": "scribal", "toenote": "", "longcitation": null}, {"id": "7989059056717910046", "text": "<html><head></head><body><p class=\"bottom_0\">Insertion in the handwriting of first unidentified scribe.</p></body></html>", "number": null, "type": "scribal", "toenote": "", "longcitation": null}, {"id": "5030802365220868726", "text": "<html><head></head><body><p class=\"bottom_0\">Insertion in the handwriting of JS.</p></body></html>", "number": null, "type": "scribal", "toenote": "", "longcitation": null}, {"id": "13487475049400922756", "text": "<html><head></head><body><p class=\"bottom_0\"><a href=\"/person/james-sloan\" class=\"referenceInPop\">James Sloan</a> overwrote and replaced JS’s original insertion.</p></body></html>", "number": null, "type": "scribal", "toenote": "", "longcitation": null}, {"id": "16623387462686388863", "text": "<html><head></head><body><p class=\"bottom_0\">Insertion in the handwriting of JS.</p></body></html>", "number": null, "type": "scribal", "toenote": "", "longcitation": null}, {"id": "7899123066019996443", "text": "<html><head></head><body><p class=\"bottom_0\">Insertion in the handwriting of JS.</p></body></html>", "number": null, "type": "scribal", "toenote": "", "longcitation": null}, {"id": "17166470754628120256", "text": "<html><head></head><body><p class=\"bottom_0\">Insertion in the handwriting of first unidentified scribe.</p></body></html>", "number": null, "type": "scribal", "toenote": "", "longcitation": null}, {"id": "14536260994903166043", "text": "<html><head></head><body><p class=\"bottom_0\">Section 6 of the state statute forbade courts from discharging a prisoner on a second writ of <a href=\"/topic/habeas-corpus\" class=\"referenceInPop\">habeas corpus</a> if he or she was charged with a criminal offence. The Nauvoo City Council added the clauses “are proven Guilty of the charges” and “if the prisoner or prisoners shall be found guilty” to the city ordinance, thus further empowering the municipal court to look behind the charges, as described above. These additions suggest that the city council misunderstood the purpose of habeas corpus, as they imply that the court would be determining guilt or innocence through the proceedings. (An Act . . . on Writs of Habeas Corpus, p. 325, sec. 6.)</p></body></html>", "number": 18, "type": "number", "toenote": "", "longcitation": "<p id=\"source-note1\"><span class=\"title\">The Revised Code of Laws, of Illinois, Enacted at the Fifth General Assembly, at Their Session Held at Vandalia, Commencing on the Fourth Day of December, 1826, and Ending the Nineteenth of February, 1827.</span> Vandalia, IL: Robert Blackwell, 1827.</p>"}, {"id": "8596433840748689106", "text": "<html><head></head><body><p class=\"bottom_0\">Insertion in the handwriting of first unidentified scribe.</p></body></html>", "number": null, "type": "scribal", "toenote": "", "longcitation": null}, {"id": "5817252757057087246", "text": "<html><head></head><body><p class=\"bottom_0\">Insertion in the handwriting of first unidentified scribe.</p></body></html>", "number": null, "type": "scribal", "toenote": "", "longcitation": null}], "meta": {"/paper-summary-PageTitle": "Ordinance, 14 November 1842, Page 11", "/paper-summary-MetaTitle": "Ordinance, 14 November 1842, Page 11", "/paper-summary-MetaDescription": "James Sloan handwriting ends; first unidentified scribe begins.Section 6. It shall not be lawful for...", "/paper-summary-MetaUrl": "/paper-summary/ordinance-14-november-1842/15", "/paper-summary-MetaImage": "/bc-jsp/content/jsp/images/11909/11909_ms16800_1_14_011_thumb.jpg"}, "scribes": [{"id": "per1363", "name": 